L16 = Lesson("1.16", "Cultura: Mississippi's Spanish Past",
    "I can describe how Spain is part of Mississippi's history.", "ACTFL Cultures, Connections",
    [("historia", "history"), ("fuerte", "fort")],
    "Is Spanish something new in Mississippi, or has it been here a long time?",
    [Text("Spanish has a long history in Mississippi. In 1540–1541, the Spanish explorer <b>Hernando de Soto</b> led an expedition through the land that is now Mississippi. Much later, Spain governed <b>Natchez</b> from 1779 to 1798, and Spain controlled the Mississippi Gulf Coast as part of Spanish West Florida until about 1810."),
     Text("In Pascagoula stands the <b>La Pointe-Krebs House</b>, often called the <b>Old Spanish Fort</b>. Despite the name, it was built by French colonists in the 1700s and is believed to be one of the oldest buildings in Mississippi. Your family's field trip there is a chance to see this history up close."),
     Callout("CULTURA HOY", "Today many Mississippians speak Spanish at home, and you can find Spanish on signs, in stores, on the radio, and at church services. Learning Spanish helps you talk with your neighbors."),
     KeyIdea("Spanish explorers and governors are part of Mississippi's story, and Spanish is part of Mississippi life today.")],
    [Problem("Which Spanish explorer passed through Mississippi in 1540–1541?", "Hernando de Soto"), Problem("Which city did Spain govern from 1779 to 1798?", "Natchez"), Problem("Who built the “Old Spanish Fort”?", "French colonists")],
    [S("Calentamiento", [SA("Respond: ¿Cómo te llamas?", "Me llamo ___."), SA("10 =", "diez")], cols=2),
     S("Practica", [SA(q, a) for q, a in [("Spanish word for fort", "fuerte"), ("Spanish word for history", "historia"), ("Where is the La Pointe-Krebs House?", "Pascagoula")]], cols=1),
     S("Conecta", [OR("Where do you see or hear Spanish in your community? List two places.", "Answers vary.", lines=2)])],
    tsp("Students connect Spanish to Mississippi history.", "Cultures and connections.", "Workbook Lesson 1.16, Unit 1 Repaso",
        "Is Spanish new here?", "Read about de Soto, Natchez, and the Gulf Coast.", "Discuss the Old Spanish Fort.", "Practica; community connections.",
        ["Assuming the Old Spanish Fort was built by Spain."], ["Timeline strip."], ["Plan questions in Spanish for the field trip."], speak="Repaso tonight; tomorrow's Examen."),
    summary="Spain is part of Mississippi's history and present.")

